# Enforce invariants mechanically, not by convention

When the system has a correctness requirement — co-occurring fields, a real infrastructure dependency, a server that must be actively running before requests arrive — enforce it through explicit, mechanical means (code assertions, required config, active polling, concrete wiring). Never rely on convention, documentation, naming, or assumed ambient behavior to maintain the invariant; implicit reliance silently fails.

## Procedures
- For state machine or orchestrator fields that must co-occur, encode the invariant as a type-level constraint or an explicit assertion that fires at construction/transition time.
- For infrastructure dependencies, always wire to the real service (Docker Compose, live socket) rather than a placeholder or simulated stand-in.
- For async dependencies (e.g. a server that must be ready), actively poll or await the readiness condition — never assume the task is reachable just because it was spawned.

